cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If EvidenceGate contributes to research or an assessment write-up, please cite it as below."
title: "EvidenceGate: repeatable evidence-package checks for security assessments"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/abdullahzarshaid/evidencegate"
url: "https://abdullahzarshaid.github.io/evidencegate/"
authors:
  - family-names: "Bin Zarshaid"
    given-names: "Abdullah"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8354-5177"
keywords:
  - security-assessment
  - evidence
  - cvss
  - penetration-testing
  - sqlite
  - python
abstract: "EvidenceGate keeps findings and evidence references in a SQLite ledger whose triggers refuse to confirm a finding with no hashed evidence, then runs deterministic checks on integrity, CVSS 3.1 vectors, HTTP capture structure, optional hostname scope and selected secret patterns. Standard library only; no network requests."
